==German==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|de|auf|machen}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈaʊ̯fˌmaxən/|[ˈʔäo̯fˌmäχən]|[-χn̩]|[-χɴ̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-aufmachen.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-aufmachen.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|auf.machen}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive}} to [[open]]
#: {{ux|de|'''Mach''' mir '''auf'''!|'''Open''' [the door] for me.}}
#: {{ux|de|Kannst du dieses Glas '''aufmachen'''?|Can you '''open''' this jar?}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|de||Aufmachen}} and {{m|de|zumachen}} are not in themselves informal. However, the formal language prefers {{m|de|öffnen}} and {{m|de|schließen}}, which are in turn rare in colloquial speech (though {{m|de||schließen}} is common in compounds like {{m|de|abschließen}}, {{m|de|zuschließen}}, etc.).

